From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a key-up after a handled key-down is prehandled

A desktop chord pressed in a `<webview>` guest is taken by
WebViewGuest::PreHandleKeyboardEvent, and RenderWidgetHostImpl then
drops every KeyUp until the next key-down, Esc's aside. The chord's
release never reached the delegate, so the shell could not report
`shortcutrelease` for it. Every KeyUp is prehandled now; it is still
not sent to the renderer.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
index e0a16f28..7ec64df0 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
@@ -1897,13 +1897,12 @@ void RenderWidgetHostImpl::ForwardKeyboardEventWithCommands(
     // If the preceding RawKeyDown event was handled by the browser, then we
     // need to suppress all events generated by it until the next RawKeyDown or
     // KeyDown event.
-    // However, always prehandle the Esc KeyUp events because they are needed to
-    // manage press-and-hold Esc key shortcuts for exiting browser fullscreen
-    // and keyboard lock.
+    // However, always prehandle KeyUp events: Esc's manages press-and-hold
+    // Esc key shortcuts for exiting browser fullscreen and keyboard lock, and
+    // Domicile's delegate lets go of the desktop chord the RawKeyDown was.
     if (key_event.GetType() == WebKeyboardEvent::Type::kKeyUp ||
         key_event.GetType() == WebKeyboardEvent::Type::kChar) {
-      if (key_event.GetType() == WebKeyboardEvent::Type::kKeyUp &&
-          key_event.windows_key_code == ui::VKEY_ESCAPE) {
+      if (key_event.GetType() == WebKeyboardEvent::Type::kKeyUp) {
         delegate_->PreHandleKeyboardEvent(key_event);
       }
       return;
